1
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,002
...Insightful as ever, Eftirvit

2
00:00:06,072 --> 00:00:09,578
I always find our discussions so rewarding

3
00:00:12,544 --> 00:00:15,666
It's just food for thought. Could be nothing

4
00:00:16,073 --> 00:00:20,850
After all, follow the logic through, and you are forced into some absurd conclusions...

5
00:00:21,564 --> 00:00:26,878
With the means to summon the essence of a complex system, the process to extract Azosite

6
00:00:27,123 --> 00:00:29,968
And technology developed to capture shooting stars...

7
00:00:31,019 --> 00:00:34,731
We may actually be able to traverse space and defy gravity...

8
00:00:35,015 --> 00:00:38,157
But that's the exciting part! My friend...

9
00:00:38,812 --> 00:00:44,727
If this theory holds, we may one day be able to summon the essence of Celestia itself

10
00:00:45,804 --> 00:00:49,463
Of course, there are plenty of technical issues to resolve first...

11
00:00:50,003 --> 00:00:53,364
We'd also need a king ambitious enough to permit it

12
00:00:53,896 --> 00:00:57,340
Your conclusion is by no means absurd

13
00:00:57,837 --> 00:01:06,972
All of spacetime is intimately connected, and a rigorous theory is like magic in a scholar's hands

14
00:01:08,474 --> 00:01:09,968
Professor, your health...

15
00:01:11,316 --> 00:01:15,483
Today is a good day. I'm feeling much better

16
00:01:15,717 --> 00:01:19,071
Thank you for your concern, Eftirvit

17
00:01:20,137 --> 00:01:22,889
I'm so happy to see you, Professor Mimameith

18
00:01:23,457 --> 00:01:28,585
We've missed having your input at the recent seminars under the tree. It's a pity

19
00:01:29,083 --> 00:01:32,681
Hehe, it's no great loss

20
00:01:33,716 --> 00:01:37,190
There is very little left that I can teach you

21
00:01:37,829 --> 00:01:44,707
In the future, I am sure you will be the very top scholars in this whole nation

22
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:54,499
My only hope is that I might live long enough to see the future you create

23
00:01:57,537 --> 00:02:01,649
How is Professor Mimameith? I heard you went to see her

24
00:02:01,927 --> 00:02:05,566
Her condition has visibly deteriorated...

25
00:02:06,265 --> 00:02:13,252
Medical treatment has no effect, nor do more direct methods of extending her lifespan. It makes no sense

26
00:02:15,497 --> 00:02:21,456
There's only one explanation... Chronic complications from His Majesty's research project

27
00:02:22,131 --> 00:02:24,962
Her health was never the same after she returned...

28
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:27,657
You mean the Abyss project?

29
00:02:28,284 --> 00:02:28,988
Yes

30
00:02:30,332 --> 00:02:34,172
I won't give up. There has to be a way...

31
00:02:34,626 --> 00:02:41,212
Professor Mimameith has always treated us like family. Whatever it takes, we must save her

32
00:02:41,658 --> 00:02:47,801
I'll use all resources at my disposal. Some of the research at the Universitas could be promising

33
00:02:48,357 --> 00:02:52,231
Uh, and about my promotion to president... I hope there's no—

34
00:02:52,231 --> 00:02:56,606
Hey, there's a time and a place. This is not it

35
00:02:58,475 --> 00:03:05,034
...You're right. My mistake, sorry... We should focus on the professor for now

36
00:03:12,991 --> 00:03:13,988
You've found a way?

37
00:03:14,967 --> 00:03:17,252
Yes. Mystery solved...

38
00:03:19,018 --> 00:03:22,758
As you know, I've been leading research into the Crimson Moon

39
00:03:23,609 --> 00:03:28,390
Recently, I discovered a more fundamental approach to extending lifespan...

40
00:03:29,348 --> 00:03:33,603
How feasible is it? How does it differ from all the previous failed methods?

41
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:40,916
This suddenly feels like a seminar under the tree, Eftirvit

42
00:03:42,295 --> 00:03:46,567
With your incisive questioning... we made so much progress back then

43
00:03:50,216 --> 00:03:55,684
But let's not waste time on theory. The results will be all the proof we need

44
00:03:56,397 --> 00:04:00,100
After all, the professor doesn't have much time left...

45
00:04:00,548 --> 00:04:03,172
Very well. I trust you, Hroptatyr

46
00:04:03,206 --> 00:04:06,439
I question only the theory, not your abilities

47
00:04:07,648 --> 00:04:09,754
Thank you, Eftirvit

48
00:04:10,770 --> 00:04:14,554
With this development, even His Majesty will be amazed

49
00:04:15,286 --> 00:04:21,461
Now, I simply deconstruct the Crimson Moon's power, and the professor will...

50
00:04:27,775 --> 00:04:30,733
What is it, Hroptatyr? What are you waiting for?

51
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:34,621
It... won't work

52
00:04:35,754 --> 00:04:39,054
The theory is flawed. I was mistaken

53
00:04:39,366 --> 00:04:44,503
...You're lying. You never doubt yourself, Hroptatyr. Explain yourself!

54
00:04:46,256 --> 00:04:51,565
It's nothing. I'll find another way. Sorry about this

55
00:04:51,821 --> 00:04:54,751
Are you worried I'll steal your work!?

56
00:04:54,951 --> 00:04:58,767
However jealous I may be of your career, I would never do such a thing!

57
00:04:58,967 --> 00:05:01,410
Our professor's life is at stake here!

58
00:05:01,610 --> 00:05:03,461
Hroptatyr! Wait...!

59
00:05:23,681 --> 00:05:26,672
Watch out, it's going to rain

